  "reason": "1) Evidence/uncertainty: No experiments have been completed, so there is zero information about which modality, encoder, profile setting, or aggregation strategy performs best. The most critical uncertainty is the absolute performance level of the simplest possible baseline, which anchors all future comparisons. 2) What this tests: config_001 (RNA-only, single profile, PCA-2000) establishes the minimal-complexity RNA baseline. It isolates the contribution of the RNA modality with a standard, fast linear encoder and no aggregation or fusion complexity. 3) Why it is the best first experiment: As the simplest configuration in the search space, it provides a clean reference point. Every subsequent experiment—varying the RNA encoder (scvi, scgpt), adding multiprofile aggregation (avgpool, transformer), adding an image modality, or testing fusion strategies—can be directly compared against this baseline to isolate the marginal effect of each design choice. Starting here maximizes the information gained per experiment under a limited budget, because it simultaneously calibrates the performance floor and sets up the clearest comparison axes for the next several runs."
